## Context

- Fiftieth run — Covered 8 projects with 10 new journal entries and 4 new tasks.
- Journal #2564 (keap1-nrf2-pancancer-dependency-atlas):
  - **VVD-065 molecular glue (Nat Chem Biol, Mar 2026).** Covalent molecular glue engages KEAP1 C151, promotes KEAP1-CUL3 complex formation, restores NRF2 degradation. Phase I open. First approach to pharmacologically restore KEAP1-mediated NRF2 suppression.
- Journal #2565 (keap1-nrf2-pancancer-dependency-atlas):
  - **NRF2 hyperactivation in HNSCC (Clin Cancer Res, Mar 2026).** KEAP1 haploinsufficiency drives radioresistance + immune suppression (PMN-MDSC recruitment, IFNy downregulation). NFE2L2 E79Q mutation amplifies effects. PMID 40742317.
- Journal #2566 (pancancer-ferroptosis-atlas):
  - **CRITICAL: Ferroptosis limits paper (bioRxiv Mar 14 2026).** Cell culture GREATLY overestimates GPX4-axis ferroptosis efficacy in vivo. GCLC inhibition triggers non-ferroptotic cystine/translation-regulated death. Principal cystine function in culture = selenoprotein support. doi:10.64898/2026.03.11.711115.
- Journal #2567 (pancancer-ferroptosis-atlas):
  - **FSP1 as persister + LN vulnerability.** Sci Adv (Jan 2 2026): persister cells downregulate FSP1, rely on residual FSP1 after GPX4i. HDACi+GPX4i/FSP1i eliminate persisters. Nature (2026, v649 pp477-486): LN hypoxia degrades GPX4; melanoma LN metastases FSP1-dependent. viFSP1/FSEN1 effective in LN only.
- Journal #2568 (swisnf-metabolic-convergence):
  - **LY4050784 SMARCA2i Phase 1 (AACR 2026).** First-in-class SMARCA2/BRM ATPase inhibitor in SMARCA4-altered solid tumors. CT109 + Abstract 3779: synergy with pembrolizumab and KRAS inhibitors. First clinical validation of SMARCA4→SMARCA2 SL paradigm.
- Journal #2569 (nf1-loss-pancancer-dependency-atlas):
  - **Daraxonrasib (RMC-6236) in NF1 neuroblastoma (bioRxiv Feb 2026).** Direct multi-RAS inhibitor effective; venetoclax combo enhances killing. **MCT Feb 2026:** Pharmacogenomic SL screens found non-MAPK NF1 targets — NF-kB, ER stress/UPR, calcium signaling. Most hits outside RAS-MAPK axis.
- Journal #2570 (wrn-msi-pancancer-atlas):
  - **WRN inhibitor resistance mapping (bioRxiv Jan 2026).** Two preprints: on-target resistance hotspots for HRO761 and VVD-214. Drug-specific profiles DIVERGE. Single-allele heterozygous mutations sufficient. DNA-PK as combination partner.
- Journal #2571 (cdkn2a-pancancer-dependency-atlas):
  - **p16/CDKN2A predicts CDK2 dependency (Nat Commun 2025).** p16 expression more predictive of CDK2i sensitivity than CCNE1. INX-315+CDK4/6i broadly active in breast PDX. Weighted mRNA signature (CCND1/CCNE1/RB1/CDKN2A) predicts response.
- Journal #2572 (tsg-co-alteration-dependency-interactions):
  - **CRISPR SL screens across 15 cancer drivers (bioRxiv Jan 2026).** Includes ARID1A and KEAP1 from our atlas series. ML paralog pair SL map. Directly supports co-alteration hypothesis.
- Journal #2573 (breast-cancer-vulnerability-stratification):
  - **MTAP-SL review (Cancer Res 2026).** Comprehensive review. Clinical agents: BMS-986504/MRTX1719, AMG 193, IDE397. Up to 45% MTAP deletion in some tumor types.
- Tasks created: research_director #1645 (URGENT ferroptosis limits evaluation, P5), #1646 (VVD-065 KEAP1/NRF2 evaluation), #1647 (WRN resistance integration); data_curator #1648 (cross-driver CRISPR SL data evaluation).
